00:06.110 --> 00:09.730
Beneath the glass ceiling of the <i>Galerie du Roy</i>,

00:10.110 --> 00:15.780
one can see the thin silhouette of a Japanese girl named Yune.

00:16.530 --> 00:22.210
For now, only a few Parisians know of her arrival...

00:35.260 --> 00:38.720
Ikoku Meiro
no Croisée

00:35.260 --> 00:38.720
The crossing in a foreign maze

00:35.260 --> 00:38.720
Paris. The end of the 19th century.
Beneath the glass ceiling of the Galerie du Roy,
one can see the thin silhouette of a Japanese girl named Yune.
For now, only a few Parisians know of her arrival...

00:35.260 --> 00:38.720
The crossing in a foreign maze

00:38.720 --> 00:44.100
As I open the gate and step out into the street

00:44.730 --> 00:48.770
asa no hikari ga mabushii

00:44.730 --> 00:48.770
朝の光が眩しい

00:44.730 --> 00:48.770
I can see the sun shining brightly

00:51.780 --> 00:56.780
doko kara ka nagareru hanauta ni

00:51.780 --> 00:56.780
どこからか流れる鼻歌に

00:51.780 --> 00:56.780
I can hear humming in the distance

00:57.950 --> 01:01.700
kokoro hazumi tokete yuku

00:57.950 --> 01:01.700
心弾み解けてゆく

00:57.950 --> 01:01.700
It moves me and melts my heart

01:04.910 --> 01:10.380
mabuta tojireba ukabu egao

01:04.910 --> 01:10.380
瞼閉じれば浮かぶ笑顔

01:04.910 --> 01:10.380
I can see that smile when I close my eyes

01:11.550 --> 01:16.970
omoidasu tabi ni namida hitotsu

01:11.550 --> 01:16.970
思い出す度に涙ひとつ

01:11.550 --> 01:16.970
It brings me to tears whenever I remember it

01:17.470 --> 01:20.600
te wo hiroge hashiridase

01:17.470 --> 01:20.600
手を広げ 走りだせ

01:17.470 --> 01:20.600
Spread your arms out and take off

01:20.600 --> 01:23.930
hi no ataru toori wo

01:20.600 --> 01:23.930
陽の当たる 通りを

01:20.600 --> 01:23.930
Down the streets where the lights shine

01:23.930 --> 01:30.480
michiyuku hito ni genki ni aisatsu

01:23.930 --> 01:30.480
道行く人に 元気に挨拶

01:23.930 --> 01:30.480
Cheerfully greet people walking down the city streets

01:30.480 --> 01:37.110
atarashii kimochi de shinkokyuu shitara

01:30.480 --> 01:37.110
新しい 気持ちで深呼吸したら

01:30.480 --> 01:37.110
Take a deep breath to refresh yourself

01:37.110 --> 01:45.620
kono sekai wa hora itsudemo kimi no mono

01:37.110 --> 01:45.620
この世界はほら いつでも 君のもの

01:37.110 --> 01:45.620
And this world will always be yours

01:51.000 --> 02:01.010
Episode 07 :

01:51.000 --> 02:01.010
" Skylight Window "

02:22.410 --> 02:24.790
<i>Didn't you hate that...?</i>

02:26.290 --> 02:30.120
<i>Well, it's not like it tastes good,</i>

02:30.120 --> 02:34.920
<i>but I thought I should try some more Japanese food.</i>

02:47.560 --> 02:50.440
Good morning, Claude-sama.

02:50.440 --> 02:51.690
Is something wrong?

02:51.690 --> 02:56.940
I just thought I should make
some more Japanese food for you.

02:59.200 --> 03:00.610
Is that...?

03:00.610 --> 03:01.320
Yes!

03:01.320 --> 03:02.700
It's umeboshi!

03:01.320 --> 03:02.700
Pickled Plums.

03:02.700 --> 03:06.120
I think I'll take my time getting used to Japanese food...

03:09.120 --> 03:09.960
Okay!

03:17.800 --> 03:19.550
What's wrong, Yune?

03:19.550 --> 03:20.670
Have you lost your appetite?

03:20.670 --> 03:23.090
No, I'm fine.

03:23.090 --> 03:24.470
I'll finish it later.

03:24.470 --> 03:27.970
It's going to get pretty tough, so you should eat it soon.

03:28.600 --> 03:30.230
Okay.

03:39.320 --> 03:40.740
That child...

03:48.120 --> 03:49.200
Wait.

03:52.580 --> 03:56.500
Hey, you shouldn't steal things anymore, okay?

03:57.750 --> 04:03.800
You wouldn't want to lose something of your own, right?

04:03.800 --> 04:06.010
Could you give that candlestick back?

04:07.890 --> 04:09.180
I sold it for bread.

04:14.100 --> 04:17.400
Here, take this.

04:17.400 --> 04:23.070
Just promise me that you won't steal or do anything that will make people sad.

04:30.290 --> 04:32.410
He's that thief from the other day, right?

04:33.580 --> 04:34.420
Yes.

04:34.420 --> 04:38.960
Buying bread for you is fine,
but he doesn't deserve a crumb from us.

04:38.960 --> 04:41.550
Are you seriously going to forgive that little thief?

04:41.550 --> 04:44.720
I told him never to do anything bad again...

04:44.720 --> 04:46.760
And you thought that he would listen?!

04:47.930 --> 04:51.600
Kids are just animals that can't understand anything.

04:52.560 --> 04:54.060
No...

04:54.060 --> 04:55.810
Wait!

04:55.810 --> 04:58.980
Children are born with pure hearts!

04:58.980 --> 05:01.610
Another one of your weird Japanese ideals?

05:01.610 --> 05:05.450
I don't know anything about Japan,
but you shouldn't underestimate the kids here.

05:05.990 --> 05:09.620
Thanks to you, our shop might become a target for thieves!

05:09.620 --> 05:11.740
I've had enough of your naivety!

05:13.250 --> 05:16.500
I'm sorry, Claude-sama...

05:21.170 --> 05:22.420
Claude...

05:22.420 --> 05:24.420
It's fine.

05:22.920 --> 05:24.420
Halt!

05:24.420 --> 05:26.380
Claude Claudel!

05:26.380 --> 05:28.800
Why are you making Yune-chan cry?!

05:28.800 --> 05:30.300
A-Alice-sama?

05:30.300 --> 05:31.970
You're here again?

05:31.970 --> 05:35.680
I'll keep coming here until you
stop bullying Yune-chan!

05:35.680 --> 05:36.520
Yune-chan!

05:36.520 --> 05:36.940
Yes?

05:36.940 --> 05:39.940
I got lots of Japanese things again!

05:39.940 --> 05:42.780
Isn't this a beautiful kanzashi?

05:42.780 --> 05:44.650
A-Alice-sama...

05:44.650 --> 05:49.160
This single hair ornament brings out so much simplicity and elegance!

05:49.160 --> 05:50.780
Um, that's...

05:52.120 --> 05:55.040
A tool used to make tea...

05:55.040 --> 05:55.790
What?

05:55.790 --> 05:57.040
I-It is?

05:58.290 --> 06:00.040
But this is...

06:04.130 --> 06:05.630
used like this, right?

06:05.630 --> 06:07.510
No, that's...

06:08.930 --> 06:11.550
a tool used to write...

06:10.510 --> 06:11.550
P
a
r
i
s

06:11.550 --> 06:12.510
Yay!

06:13.560 --> 06:16.350
Th-Then, this is...

06:17.980 --> 06:19.310
a sink, right?

06:19.310 --> 06:20.600
No!

06:21.360 --> 06:24.190
You use it like this!

06:28.900 --> 06:31.950
All right, you can go home already.

06:32.530 --> 06:33.620
I'm not going home!

06:33.620 --> 06:35.540
Are you trying to keep Yune-chan all to yourself?

06:35.200 --> 06:36.080
Um-

06:35.540 --> 06:36.540
Just go home!

06:36.080 --> 06:38.750
I'm not going home!

06:36.540 --> 06:38.750
You're disrupting our business!

06:39.330 --> 06:45.000
Milady, Yune doesn't feel so well today, so it would be best if you went home for the day.

06:45.000 --> 06:47.090
Is that so, Yune-chan?

06:47.090 --> 06:48.420
Are you all right?

06:49.170 --> 06:51.220
Yes, I'm fine.

06:53.100 --> 06:54.510
All right then,

06:54.510 --> 06:56.930
I guess I'll go home for today.

06:58.600 --> 07:00.350
Have a nice day,

07:00.350 --> 07:01.690
Yune-chan.

07:06.530 --> 07:08.240
What's wrong, Yune-chan?!

07:08.240 --> 07:11.740
There's no <i>bise</i> in Japanese culture, Milady.

07:11.740 --> 07:12.950
Really?

07:13.700 --> 07:20.460
Well, if you're that startled, it must mean that I've become much more closer to you than these other people!

07:21.120 --> 07:26.460
That was a <i>bise</i>, a common greeting between close friends.

07:26.460 --> 07:31.470
If nobody's done it to you before,
they probably haven't accepted you yet!

07:32.260 --> 07:34.930
Get out of this place and come live with me!

07:34.930 --> 07:37.140
Go home already!

07:37.140 --> 07:40.730
You don't have to push me out!

07:40.730 --> 07:42.730
<i>You're</i> the pushy one!

07:43.440 --> 07:45.310
I can't take my eyes off of her for a minute.

07:46.110 --> 07:50.610
You should rest if you aren't feeling well, Yune.

07:50.610 --> 07:52.740
I really am fine.

07:52.740 --> 07:54.740
I'm sorry to have worried you.

08:13.130 --> 08:17.300
Sorry, I can't give you anything else.

08:17.300 --> 08:20.100
My master scolded me.

08:26.810 --> 08:28.940
Please understand.

08:28.940 --> 08:30.940
We can't see each other anymore,

08:30.940 --> 08:34.150
but remember: you're not alone.

08:38.580 --> 08:40.040
Good luck.

08:40.040 --> 08:41.200
Yune!

08:46.500 --> 08:50.500
Do you have any idea what you've done?

08:50.500 --> 08:52.130
I'm sorry.

08:52.130 --> 08:53.760
I was bidding farewell.

08:53.760 --> 08:55.010
Farewell?

08:55.010 --> 08:58.140
You only do that with close friends!

08:58.140 --> 09:00.810
Do you want more thieves coming to our shop?

09:00.810 --> 09:06.060
Maybe you're sick because of his germs!

09:06.060 --> 09:07.350
Please stop!

09:07.350 --> 09:08.730
Don't say that!

09:09.980 --> 09:13.490
He's doing his best to get by.

09:15.110 --> 09:18.620
I'll promise that I'll never meet him again,

09:18.620 --> 09:26.250
but please understand that he's searching all over Paris for a place to live.

09:28.330 --> 09:32.000
I know I'm being selfish,

09:32.500 --> 09:39.510
but I want to understand how he feels.

09:41.760 --> 09:44.730
I don't understand how you can be so stubborn,

09:44.730 --> 09:47.520
but just promise me this:

09:47.520 --> 09:49.440
You'll never go near him again.

09:53.030 --> 09:56.990
Yes, Claude-sama.

10:33.110 --> 10:34.020
Yune!

10:34.020 --> 10:34.900
What's wrong?!

10:34.900 --> 10:36.030
Yune?

10:36.030 --> 10:36.820
Yune?!

10:48.330 --> 10:51.040
She was fine up until now.

10:51.040 --> 10:53.000
She collapsed right after our argument.

10:53.500 --> 10:55.130
Is it my fault?

10:55.130 --> 10:56.510
Don't blame yourself.

10:56.510 --> 10:59.760
Yune was probably just acting like she was okay.

11:01.800 --> 11:04.560
It's my fault.

11:05.510 --> 11:09.060
This is not your fault, Claude-sama.

11:10.520 --> 11:12.730
Should we go to the hospital?

11:12.730 --> 11:16.320
It's fine. I can get over this myself.

11:16.820 --> 11:22.070
I cannot cause you any more trouble.

11:25.080 --> 11:27.160
I'll go call a doctor,

11:27.160 --> 11:28.040
so-

11:29.910 --> 11:32.040
It's just a cold, right?

11:32.040 --> 11:33.420
What do you mean?

11:33.420 --> 11:35.670
Is she hiding something from us?

11:35.670 --> 11:37.920
She tends to do that.

11:37.920 --> 11:41.970
She acted like she didn't know French when she came here.

11:41.970 --> 11:45.510
That was just your assumption, Claude.

11:47.180 --> 11:52.350
You just need to let Yune rest for now.

12:05.660 --> 12:07.280
You won't find her here.

12:09.200 --> 12:10.660
She collapsed.

12:13.870 --> 12:16.170
It might be your fault!

12:21.300 --> 12:22.550
Damn it.

12:26.640 --> 12:27.640
<i>Yune?</i>

12:28.640 --> 12:29.890
<i>Yune?</i>

12:31.140 --> 12:32.100
<i>Yune...</i>

12:37.730 --> 12:39.400
<i>Nee-sama...</i>

12:43.740 --> 12:48.780
<i>Your hand feels nice and cold.</i>

12:51.540 --> 12:53.750
<i>Here's some hot ginger tea that Mother made.</i>

12:53.750 --> 12:58.250
<i>Your cold will go away in a flash if you drink this.</i>

13:30.910 --> 13:32.410
<i>Please stop!</i>

13:32.410 --> 13:34.410
<i>Don't say that!</i>

13:34.410 --> 13:37.620
<i>He's doing his best to get by.</i>

13:37.620 --> 13:40.340
<i>I know I'm being selfish,</i>

13:40.340 --> 13:47.800
<i>but I want to understand how he feels.</i>

13:48.680 --> 13:54.850
<i>he's looking all over Paris for a place to live.</i>

14:00.560 --> 14:03.190
Yune's the one that's looking all over Paris.

14:03.190 --> 14:07.900
She saw herself in that kid...

14:09.490 --> 14:14.450
The hospital's too crowded for any-

14:14.450 --> 14:18.330
Is living here too hard on Yune?

14:18.330 --> 14:19.080
What?

14:19.080 --> 14:24.210
It has to be. She came from a completely different country, after all.

14:24.210 --> 14:25.920
What are you talking about?

14:26.630 --> 14:29.130
It might be best if Yune goes back to Japan.

14:30.510 --> 14:32.430
That's what's probably best for Yune.

14:32.430 --> 14:36.220
I could even go with her.

14:36.850 --> 14:38.730
You're always like this.

14:38.730 --> 14:41.730
Doesn't Yune have a say in this?

14:41.730 --> 14:42.520
Hey!

14:46.900 --> 14:48.490
I'm coming in, Yune.

14:50.950 --> 14:52.410
Yune!

14:53.280 --> 14:54.160
Are you all right?

15:04.840 --> 15:09.590
That book never did any good.

15:10.510 --> 15:16.350
You had already studied French yourself.
There was no need for me to buy that book...

15:28.610 --> 15:29.490
Hey,

15:29.490 --> 15:30.990
where are you going?!

15:35.990 --> 15:41.830
What could possibly bring you here on your own?

15:41.830 --> 15:43.790
Yune collapsed.

15:43.790 --> 15:44.840
What?

15:44.840 --> 15:48.210
I'm begging you! Please get us a doctor.

15:48.210 --> 15:49.340
I'll pay the fee.

15:49.340 --> 15:52.680
What did you do to my precious Yune-chan?!

15:52.680 --> 15:55.010
Edgar, call a doctor now!

15:55.010 --> 15:56.720
Yes, Milady.

15:58.470 --> 15:59.640
Thank you.

16:01.520 --> 16:04.100
I also have one more thing to ask.

16:07.730 --> 16:09.650
Thanks again.

16:42.770 --> 16:43.690
Claude...

16:44.520 --> 16:45.810
How's Yune?

16:45.810 --> 16:47.690
Much better.

16:50.280 --> 16:53.490
I asked Alice for a doctor.

16:53.490 --> 16:57.030
You asked Lady Alice?!

16:59.490 --> 17:03.000
This should be fine, right?

17:03.000 --> 17:03.660
Ow!

17:04.710 --> 17:08.170
Is this really what it's supposed to taste like?!

17:05.170 --> 17:08.170
I guess there's nothing to worry about.

17:19.800 --> 17:20.600
What?

17:20.600 --> 17:22.520
The recipe for rice porridge?

17:22.520 --> 17:23.730
Yes.

17:23.730 --> 17:29.440
He bowed deeply, asking for a recipe for a Japanese food for sick people.

17:29.440 --> 17:32.440
I told him, and even wrote it down for him.

17:32.440 --> 17:35.820
Oh, Claude did?

17:38.450 --> 17:41.030
This isn't something to laugh about, Onee-sama!

17:41.030 --> 17:43.040
I can't lose to him!

17:43.040 --> 17:45.960
I'll do anything for Yune-chan!

17:53.340 --> 17:54.840
How're you feeling?

17:54.840 --> 17:57.880
I feel much better now.

17:57.880 --> 17:59.840
It seems it was just a cold.

17:59.840 --> 18:04.600
The doctor said a healthy meal and some rest should do the trick.

18:05.230 --> 18:08.480
I'm sorry for causing you so much trouble.

18:10.610 --> 18:13.110
Rice porridge?

18:13.110 --> 18:19.570
Yep, Claude went to the Blanche family and begged for the recipe.

18:19.570 --> 18:20.320
Grandpa!

18:20.950 --> 18:22.700
You did all of that for me...

18:22.700 --> 18:25.330
Alice brought the doctor, too.

18:26.830 --> 18:28.750
Really?

18:29.370 --> 18:32.250
Anyway, I think this is for you.

18:35.130 --> 18:36.590
It's from that kid.

18:37.760 --> 18:39.760
It's a terribly miserable weed,

18:40.590 --> 18:44.720
but he's pretty smart.

18:47.230 --> 18:49.850
Wh-What? Did I do something wrong again?!

18:49.850 --> 18:54.230
No, thank you very much.

18:54.230 --> 18:56.610
You shouldn't cry, then.

18:56.610 --> 19:02.120
I'm just so happy to have received these gifts

19:02.120 --> 19:05.870
from Claude-sama and that boy...

19:06.750 --> 19:13.750
This flower is so tiny and beat up.

19:13.750 --> 19:18.630
I can imagine him working so hard to pick this.

19:19.510 --> 19:21.890
You seem happier than when you saw my porridge.

19:22.640 --> 19:24.260
I-I'm sorry!

19:24.260 --> 19:27.770
I'm also very thankful for that, Claude-sama!

19:27.770 --> 19:31.850
Whatever, just eat up and get to sleep.

19:31.850 --> 19:33.810
Ah, I can do-

19:38.820 --> 19:41.610
Here, eat.

19:41.610 --> 19:42.860
Okay.

19:50.870 --> 19:52.750
It's delicious!

20:11.850 --> 20:13.900
Thank you very much.

20:14.480 --> 20:16.980
You're far too reserved.

20:16.980 --> 20:18.860
He's right, Yune.

20:18.860 --> 20:21.490
You can rely on us a bit more.

20:21.490 --> 20:25.620
Okay, but I've already recovered.

20:25.620 --> 20:28.280
Please go back to work.

20:28.280 --> 20:29.790
Are we a nuisance?

20:29.790 --> 20:31.620
No!

20:32.250 --> 20:38.750
I just think that if you stay here for
too long, you might catch my cold.

20:40.710 --> 20:44.340
You don't have to worry about anything!

20:44.340 --> 20:45.970
Just go to sleep!

20:45.970 --> 20:50.270
We don't mind if you cause some trouble.

21:02.990 --> 21:09.120
We're the only family you have in Paris.

21:20.920 --> 21:21.670
Right!

21:33.930 --> 21:40.520
aa marude yume wo miteru you na

21:33.930 --> 21:40.520
ああ、まるで夢を見てるような

21:33.930 --> 21:40.520
Ah, it's as if I'm in a dream

21:40.520 --> 21:46.320
yawarakana hikari no naka de

21:40.520 --> 21:46.320
柔らかな光の中で

21:40.520 --> 21:46.320
As I lie here in this tender light

21:46.320 --> 21:57.330
me wo tojite mimi wo sumasereba kikoete kuru

21:46.320 --> 21:57.330
目を閉じて耳を澄ませれば　聞こえてくる

21:46.320 --> 21:57.330
When I close my eyes and listen, I can hear it

21:59.170 --> 22:12.220
atatakaku watashi wo yobu yasashii sono koe ga

21:59.170 --> 22:12.220
あたたかく私を呼ぶ優しいその声が

21:59.170 --> 22:12.220
That kind voice that warmly calls to me

22:14.810 --> 22:21.400
afureru omoi wo tsutaetai kono te kara

22:14.810 --> 22:21.400
溢れる思いを伝えたい　この手から

22:14.810 --> 22:21.400
I want to extend my feelings with these hands

22:21.400 --> 22:27.700
kotoba ja nakute kokoro de tsunagaru

22:21.400 --> 22:27.700
言葉じゃなくて　心で繋がる

22:21.400 --> 22:27.700
We connect through our hearts, not our words

22:27.700 --> 22:34.370
hajimeyou koko kara sodateyou nukumori wo

22:27.700 --> 22:34.370
始めよう　ここから育てよう　温もりを

22:27.700 --> 22:34.370
Let's begin here. Let's nurture the warmth

22:34.370 --> 22:40.830
atarashii hibi ga watashi wo matteru

22:34.370 --> 22:40.830
新しい日々が私を待ってる

22:34.370 --> 22:40.830
A new day is waiting for me

22:40.830 --> 22:54.560
mamoru mono wa kitto koko ni aru no

22:40.830 --> 22:54.560
守るものはきっとここにあるの

22:40.830 --> 22:54.560
I'm sure there is something here for me to protect

23:03.230 --> 23:04.520
Yune-chan!

23:04.520 --> 23:06.730
Ice works the best for a cold!

23:06.730 --> 23:08.740
Doesn't it feel so nice and cold?

23:08.740 --> 23:12.740
Your fever should go away in a flash!

23:14.120 --> 23:17.750
In Japan, we warm up and sweat our colds away...

23:17.750 --> 23:19.000
R-Really?!

23:19.000 --> 23:20.420
What about an ice bath?

23:20.420 --> 23:21.500
I'll pass!

23:21.500 --> 23:22.920
Go home!

23:35.050 --> 23:36.140
Next episode:

23:35.260 --> 23:40.810
Episode 08 :

23:36.140 --> 23:37.470
Kid's Room.

23:37.470 --> 23:38.680
Please watch it.
